<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-26T19:26:27+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:26:27 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Archaeologists digging ahead of an electricity substation found more than 200 Celtic coins]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136157513.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Hungary, the discovery of over 200 Celtic silver coins during excavations for a new electricity substation is creating quite a buzz. These coins, which date back more than 2,000 years, are a remarkable testament to the region's ancient history. Additionally, the site revealed a Roman villa and prehistoric tools, showcasing thousands of years of human activity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/archaeologists-digging-ahead-of-an-electricity-substation-in-western-hungary-found-more-than-200-celtic-silver-coins-packed-in-a-small-clay-pot-40cm-underground-the-largest-such-hoard-there-in-over-50-years/articleshow/136157513.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/archaeologists-digging-ahead-of-an-electricity-substation-in-western-hungary-found-more-than-200-celtic-silver-coins-packed-in-a-small-clay-pot-40cm-underground-the-largest-such-hoard-there-in-over-50-years/articleshow/136157513.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T18:52:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136157979,imgsize-246386.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Louisiana father’s decision to give farm to brother upheld after children challenge inheritance]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136193275.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Louisiana, a father's decision to transfer property to his brother, while retaining a lifetime residency right, sparked a legal battle after his death. His children contested the transfer, alleging it undermined their inheritance rights. However, the court found a lack of proof regarding inadequate living resources. The appeals court upheld the transfer, affirming the father's legal rights and the validity of his gift to his brother.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-louisiana-father-gave-his-farm-and-home-to-his-brother-in-2014-while-keeping-the-right-to-live-there-for-life-after-he-died-his-younger-children-challenged-the-transfer-but-an-appeals-court-left-it-intact/articleshow/136193275.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-louisiana-father-gave-his-farm-and-home-to-his-brother-in-2014-while-keeping-the-right-to-live-there-for-life-after-he-died-his-younger-children-challenged-the-transfer-but-an-appeals-court-left-it-intact/articleshow/136193275.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T18:49:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136193507,imgsize-2259614.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Forsythe Farm Demolition Halt: Court pauses demolition; group must post $25,000 bond by November 30]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136155473.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Commonwealth Court has stepped in, imposing a temporary pause on Forsythe Farm's demolition while an appeal is considered. To prolong this halt, Save Forsythe Farm must secure $25,000 by November 30. Currently, they've garnered over $7,000 via a GoFundMe campaign aiming for $35,000. Due to safety concerns and the building's decline, West Goshen Township sought legal action.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-judge-temporarily-stopped-demolition-of-an-8-5-acre-historic-farmhouse-but-residents-must-raise-25000-by-november-30-to-keep-it-standing-while-they-fight-for-a-chance-to-save-the-building/articleshow/136155473.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-judge-temporarily-stopped-demolition-of-an-8-5-acre-historic-farmhouse-but-residents-must-raise-25000-by-november-30-to-keep-it-standing-while-they-fight-for-a-chance-to-save-the-building/articleshow/136155473.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T18:52:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136155532,imgsize-1394467.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Family farm dispute: Canadian court rules son owns one-third after parents added him to title in 2008]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136161043.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2008, a Canadian couple designated their son's name on the family farm title, granting him a share in ownership. As family ties deteriorated, a dispute arose over farm ownership between the parents and the son. The Manitoba Court of Appeal upheld the son's one-third stake in the property, rejecting the parents' previous claims and ordering the sale of the farm as per the Law of Property Act.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-canadian-couple-added-their-son-to-the-title-of-their-family-farm-in-2008-but-a-falling-out-15-years-later-led-to-a-legal-battle-an-appeals-court-has-now-recognised-his-one-third-share-and-ordered-a-sale/articleshow/136161043.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-canadian-couple-added-their-son-to-the-title-of-their-family-farm-in-2008-but-a-falling-out-15-years-later-led-to-a-legal-battle-an-appeals-court-has-now-recognised-his-one-third-share-and-ordered-a-sale/articleshow/136161043.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T18:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136161094,imgsize-1418648.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Taylor Swift wore a long-discontinued aquarium T-shirt in 'The Life of a Showgirl' film promotion, inspiring fans to revive the 32-year-old design and raise more than $2 million for sea otter conservation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136184365.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/taylor-swift-wore-a-long-discontinued-aquarium-t-shirt-in-the-life-of-a-showgirl-film-promotion-inspiring-fans-to-revive-the-32-year-old-design-and-raise-more-than-2-million-for-sea-otter-conservation/articleshow/136184365.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/taylor-swift-wore-a-long-discontinued-aquarium-t-shirt-in-the-life-of-a-showgirl-film-promotion-inspiring-fans-to-revive-the-32-year-old-design-and-raise-more-than-2-million-for-sea-otter-conservation/articleshow/136184365.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T14:11:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136184596,imgsize-1755680.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Titanic sub disaster sparks $50 million lawsuit against OceanGate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136191448.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/five-people-never-returned-from-a-titanic-expedition-in-2023-more-than-50-million-lawsuit-filed-by-french-explorer-paul-henri-nargeolets-estate-questions-oceangates-safety-decisions-and-the-construction-of-its-doomed-submersible/articleshow/136191448.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/five-people-never-returned-from-a-titanic-expedition-in-2023-more-than-50-million-lawsuit-filed-by-french-explorer-paul-henri-nargeolets-estate-questions-oceangates-safety-decisions-and-the-construction-of-its-doomed-submersible/articleshow/136191448.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T17:50:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136191614,imgsize-1225671.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Joshua Kutryk watches Katherine’s birth from ISS; her name honours his capsule]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136191045.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Canadian astronaut Joshua Kutryk experienced a unique moment in his life when he witnessed the birth of his daughter, Katherine Grace, from the International Space Station. While his wife Heather welcomed their baby in Houston on November 24, 2026, Kutryk celebrated this milestone with mixed emotions, as he was unable to join them.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/canadian-astronaut-joshua-kutryk-watches-the-birth-of-daughter-katherine-grace-from-the-international-space-station-her-name-honours-the-capsule-that-carried-him-to-orbit/articleshow/136191045.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/canadian-astronaut-joshua-kutryk-watches-the-birth-of-daughter-katherine-grace-from-the-international-space-station-her-name-honours-the-capsule-that-carried-him-to-orbit/articleshow/136191045.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T17:41:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136191138,imgsize-1539301.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Army calls Iowa blast of nearly 5 tonnes of toxic explosives a ‘huge success’ after health fears]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136191702.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-army-calls-iowa-blast-of-nearly-5-tonnes-of-toxic-explosives-a-huge-success-after-health-fears/articleshow/136191702.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-army-calls-iowa-blast-of-nearly-5-tonnes-of-toxic-explosives-a-huge-success-after-health-fears/articleshow/136191702.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T18:00:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136191929,imgsize-57456.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Court upholds order to move utility pole after years-long neighbour dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136159256.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Connecticut appeals court has upheld an order requiring neighbours to authorise the removal of a utility pole that has blocked two homeowners from widening their driveway, ending a legal dispute that began in 2019.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-connecticut-homeowners-went-to-court-in-2019-over-a-utility-pole-that-prevented-them-from-widening-their-driveway-seven-years-later-an-appeals-court-upheld-an-order-requiring-neighbours-to-authorise-removal/articleshow/136159256.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/two-connecticut-homeowners-went-to-court-in-2019-over-a-utility-pole-that-prevented-them-from-widening-their-driveway-seven-years-later-an-appeals-court-upheld-an-order-requiring-neighbours-to-authorise-removal/articleshow/136159256.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T17:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136159795,imgsize-320420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Titus O'Neil's foundation brings Thanksgiving meals to 500 Tampa families]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136160353.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Titus O'Neil joined forces with Metropolitan Ministries to provide 500 Thanksgiving food boxes to families in Tampa, demonstrating a commitment to community support. The event, hosted at the Thaddeus M. Bullard Academy, saw the involvement of over 50 volunteers. Each box was packed with traditional meal essentials for four to six individuals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wwe-star-titus-oneil-grew-up-knowing-what-it-meant-to-need-food-assistance-his-foundation-has-now-teamed-with-a-tampa-charity-to-give-500-families-thanksgiving-boxes-each-containing-meals-for-four-to-six-people/articleshow/136160353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/wwe-star-titus-oneil-grew-up-knowing-what-it-meant-to-need-food-assistance-his-foundation-has-now-teamed-with-a-tampa-charity-to-give-500-families-thanksgiving-boxes-each-containing-meals-for-four-to-six-people/articleshow/136160353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T17:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136160416,imgsize-1000207.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Professor loses $475K case to assistant; Nevada home faces court-ordered sale]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136189453.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-retired-nevada-professor-lost-a-475000-battery-case-to-his-former-assistant-after-a-workplace-altercation-years-later-he-fought-to-block-the-court-ordered-sale-of-his-nevada-home-to-recover-the-judgment/articleshow/136189453.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-retired-nevada-professor-lost-a-475000-battery-case-to-his-former-assistant-after-a-workplace-altercation-years-later-he-fought-to-block-the-court-ordered-sale-of-his-nevada-home-to-recover-the-judgment/articleshow/136189453.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T16:54:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136189638,imgsize-229232.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida jury awards $6M to family of man who died during elective neck surgery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136155315.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-jury-awarded-6-million-to-the-wife-and-two-daughters-of-carlos-chalbaud-who-died-on-the-operating-table-during-elective-neck-surgery-at-holy-cross-hospital-without-clearance-from-a-cardiologist/articleshow/136155315.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-jury-awarded-6-million-to-the-wife-and-two-daughters-of-carlos-chalbaud-who-died-on-the-operating-table-during-elective-neck-surgery-at-holy-cross-hospital-without-clearance-from-a-cardiologist/articleshow/136155315.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T04:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136155360,imgsize-802985.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Britain net migration falls to 77,000, lowest level since 1997 outside pandemic]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136187456.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/britain-net-migration-falls-to-77000-lowest-level-since-1997-outside-pandemic/articleshow/136187456.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/britain-net-migration-falls-to-77000-lowest-level-since-1997-outside-pandemic/articleshow/136187456.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T15:56:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136187795,imgsize-1947581.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Alaska pilot drops frozen turkeys from her plane to remote families, reviving Thanksgiving tradition]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136159875.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Esther Keim has taken up a beloved tradition of delivering frozen turkeys to isolated families in Alaska, initially inspired by the generous actions of local pilot Kenny Hughes. In 2022, her inaugural delivery saw 36 turkeys spread over a vast 75 miles. With growing community support and volunteer involvement, Keim aims to significantly expand the initiative to benefit even more villages in the coming years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-alaska-pilot-who-grew-up-in-a-village-with-no-roads-or-shops-revived-an-old-thanksgiving-tradition-in-her-single-engine-plane-dropping-frozen-turkeys-in-burlap-sacks-to-remote-families-every-year-since-2022/articleshow/136159875.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-alaska-pilot-who-grew-up-in-a-village-with-no-roads-or-shops-revived-an-old-thanksgiving-tradition-in-her-single-engine-plane-dropping-frozen-turkeys-in-burlap-sacks-to-remote-families-every-year-since-2022/articleshow/136159875.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T16:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136160195,imgsize-768001.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Congo Ebola outbreak crosses 12,000 cases as fighting disrupts response]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136187000.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The ongoing Ebola outbreak in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo has now surpassed 12,000 confirmed cases since May. Armed conflicts in the area are significantly obstructing containment efforts and hampering the work of health teams. Tragically, nearly half of those infected have died, marking this as the most deadly outbreak ever recorded in the country.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/congo-ebola-outbreak-crosses-12000-cases-as-fighting-disrupts-response/articleshow/136187000.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/congo-ebola-outbreak-crosses-12000-cases-as-fighting-disrupts-response/articleshow/136187000.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T15:51:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136187358,imgsize-125404.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[4 dead, 17 missing after six-storey building collapses in Pakistan's Karachi]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136186755.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On Wednesday, a six-storey under-construction building in Karachi collapsed, killing at least four and injuring 14 individuals. Rescue efforts continued into Thursday to locate 17 more individuals believed to be trapped under the debris. The building was reportedly erected illegally on a site designated for residential use, prompting official concerns. Sindh Chief Minister Murad Ali Shah ordered the removal of several officials for alleged negligence in construction oversight.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/4-dead-17-missing-after-six-storey-building-collapses-in-pakistans-karachi/articleshow/136186755.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/4-dead-17-missing-after-six-storey-building-collapses-in-pakistans-karachi/articleshow/136186755.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T15:30:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136186905,imgsize-195874.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['We were told he was under no investigation': JD Vance on Nvidia CEO Huang amid China spy claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136186283.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/we-were-told-he-was-under-no-investigation-jd-vance-on-nvidia-ceo-huang-amid-china-spy-claims/articleshow/136186283.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/we-were-told-he-was-under-no-investigation-jd-vance-on-nvidia-ceo-huang-amid-china-spy-claims/articleshow/136186283.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T15:11:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136186368,imgsize-1288907.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Japan travel warning: UK embassy flags drink-spiking, credit card fraud targeting tourists in Tokyo]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136188361.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/japan-travel-warning-uk-embassy-flags-drink-spiking-credit-card-fraud-targeting-tourists-in-tokyo/articleshow/136188361.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/japan-travel-warning-uk-embassy-flags-drink-spiking-credit-card-fraud-targeting-tourists-in-tokyo/articleshow/136188361.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T16:26:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136188703,imgsize-95635.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian fish hatchery that failed to raise barramundi for five years released 3,000 young fish]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136155962.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After five years of failing to produce barramundi, the Les Wilson Barramundi Discovery Centre has successfully bred 3,000 fingerlings. David Hammann, who lacks formal aquaculture training, led the turnaround by experimenting with breeding techniques. The fingerlings are crucial for restocking local waterways and ensuring a sustainable fish population. Local fishing groups anticipate improvement in lake populations as they await more fingerlings in the future.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-fish-hatchery-that-had-failed-to-raise-barramundi-for-more-than-five-years-finally-released-3000-young-fish-into-gulf-wetlands-after-a-former-commercial-fisher-reworked-the-breeding-programme/articleshow/136155962.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/an-australian-fish-hatchery-that-had-failed-to-raise-barramundi-for-more-than-five-years-finally-released-3000-young-fish-into-gulf-wetlands-after-a-former-commercial-fisher-reworked-the-breeding-programme/articleshow/136155962.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T15:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136156089,imgsize-93674.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[£1 charity shop ring turns out to be rare £2,000 Mughal gold treasure]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136158701.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[While browsing a charity shop, a woman stumbled upon a ring priced at just £1, assuming it was merely costume jewellery. To her astonishment, when featured on the BBC's Antiques Roadshow, expert John Benjamin revealed its true worth. Dating back to the Georgian period, this 22-carat gold Mughal ring boasted a diamond and ruby stones, proving that hidden treasures often lie in the most unexpected places.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-woman-bought-a-ring-for-1-at-a-british-charity-shop-believing-it-was-costume-jewellery-an-expert-discovered-it-was-a-22-carat-gold-mughal-ring-with-diamonds-and-rubies-worth-2000/articleshow/136158701.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-woman-bought-a-ring-for-1-at-a-british-charity-shop-believing-it-was-costume-jewellery-an-expert-discovered-it-was-a-22-carat-gold-mughal-ring-with-diamonds-and-rubies-worth-2000/articleshow/136158701.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-26T15:01:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136158791,imgsize-474719.cms"/></item></channel></rss>